  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 9, 2026, three influential figures within the Indonesian Solidarity Party (PSI)—Giring Ganesha, Raja Juli Antoni, and Isyana Bagoes Oka—announced their resignations from the political organization. These departures occurred simultaneously, drawing significant attention from national media outlets. According to reports, the individuals stated that their decision to leave the party was motivated by a desire to focus exclusively on their ongoing duties and obligations within the government. The leadership of PSI, including party head Kaesang Pangarep, has responded to the resignations calmly. While the move represents a notable shift in the party's composition, the individuals involved emphasized that the transition is necessary to manage their official governmental portfolios effectively. Public discourse also touched upon broader political discussions, including separate calls from other political entities regarding the resignation of government officials.",
